    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about efficiency, but it feels like you're still kind of brushing off the actual impact on the current residents. if a neighborhood already has a school at 95% capacity, adding 500 units is going to cause an immediate issue, regardless of the long-term per-capita math. isn't it a bit dismissive to call those \"misapplied fears\" when they're dealing with real-time resource shortages? isn't there a legitimate way to argue that density can be actually harmful to the stability of an existing community?",
